    "alert_id": "EX3_003",
    "title": "Dyslipidemia and hyperglycemia screening under DTG",
    "message": "Guidelines require hyperglycemia screening for DTG patients with ≥2 risk factors (age ≥30, BMI ≥25). Patient has both risk factors plus BMI 33. Fasting glucose 5.6 mmol/L is borderline. LDL 4.2, total cholesterol 6.4, and triglycerides 2.3 mmol/L are all elevated. Uncontrolled hypothyroidism is a known cause of secondary dyslipidemia and may also affect glucose metabolism, compounding DTG metabolic risks. The clinician's plan does not address monitoring or managing these metabolic abnormalities.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
