    "alert_id": "EX3_004",
    "title": "Overdue TDF renal monitoring",
    "message": "Guidelines require serum creatinine and eGFR monitoring every 12 months for patients on TDF. The last creatinine was 196 days ago (2025-08-12), so annual monitoring is not yet overdue but is approaching. The clinician's plan does not include renal monitoring today despite the patient being on TDF for 3 years. TDF can cause chronic kidney disease, Fanconi syndrome, and decreased bone mineral density. Current creatinine of 72 umol/L appears acceptable, but no eGFR was documented.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "low",
    "recommended_action": "Ensure serum creatinine and eGFR are checked at or before the 12-month mark from the last test (due by August 2026). Document eGFR with creatinine results.",
